Phil 3:1 , He warns them to beware of the false teachers of the circumcision;
Phil 3:4 , shewing that himself has greater cause than they to trust in the righteousness of the law;
Phil 3:7 , which notwithstanding he counts as dung and loss, to gain Christ and his righteousness;
Phil 3:12 , therein acknowledging his own imperfection;
Phil 3:15 , He exhorts them to be thus minded;
Phil 3:17 , and to imitate him
Phil 3:18 . and to decline the ways of carnal Christians.
